  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 358 AM EDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nMonday through Thursday Night...|\n\nThe overall forecast remains on track for the strong 594 dm 500mb \nridge to continue to build and shift eastward over the Ohio Valley \nby the middle of next week. This will continue to keep us dry with \ndaily max temperatures gradually increasing each day. While we will \nsee increased low-level moisture, daily afternoon dry air mix down \nwill result in dewpoints in the upper 60s with a few locations into \nthe low 70s. Latest LREF show a 60-80% probability of heat index \nvalues over 100 for Tuesday through Thursday. Given the long \nduration of 90+ degree highs, warm overnight temperatures and daily \nheat index values near or slightly below the 105 Heat Advisory \ncriteria and after collaborating with our neighboring offices, heat \nrelated headlines will likely be needed. \n\nAs was pointed out in the previous discussion, a few areas in our \nCWA like those over the Bluegrass where there has been higher than \nnormal precipitation over the last 30 days, could result in lower \nhigh temperatures due to evaporation of moisture in the ground and \nvegetation. Other areas along and west of I-65 and points south have \nthe higher probability of seeing hotter temperatures over the next \nseveral days. \n\nEnd of the Week into Next Weekend...\n\nDeterministic models continue to show the upper level ridge \nflattening and retrograde slightly westward.  A back door frontal \nboundary may try and attempt to drop south into the region and \nstalls. NBM guidance continues to show widespread 30% PoP both \nFriday and Saturday for isolated to scattered showers and \nthunderstorms but overall confidence remains low.",
